Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

&amp;nbsp;






 PRINTERSCLAN





 &amp;nbsp;





 &amp;nbsp;


 &amp;nbsp;



 Dear gh We hope this email finds you well.
 We appreciate you reaching out about issues with your
 HP printer
 5684








 Error code or Error message




 1. Check Power and Connections




 Make sure the printer is turned on
 and properly connected to both the power outlet and your
 computer.







 2. Restart the Printer





 Press and hold down the power button on your printer till
 all the lights turn off &amp; the printer is shut down.

 Wait for 10-15 seconds and press the power button again
 to restart the Printer.









 3. Hard Reset the Printer





 a) Shut down the printer &amp; disconnect the printer from
 the power source by removing the power cable.
 b) Wait for 30 seconds. Reconnect it to the power source
 and turn on the printer.








 4. Connect Wirelessly




 a) Press and hold down the wireless connection button on
 your printer till the wifi lights start flashing.
 b) You will see the network settings on your printer
 screen.
 c) Choose the name of your network and enter the network
 password.








 5. Reinstall the Cartridge




 a) Turn off your printer.

 b) Remove the cartridges from the printer.
 c) Shake them well and reinstall them and turn on the
 printer again.








 6. Paper Jam





 Remove the printer tray and check for any piece of paper
 stuck inside.
 Make sure you are entering the correct size of paper in
 the tray and it’s inserted in the right manner.
 If your print job isn&#039;t coming out, check the print queue
 on your computer to ensure the job is not stuck or
 paused.








 7. Paper and Ink/Toner





 Ensure that there is enough paper in the tray and that
 the ink or toner cartridges are not empty or dried out.









 8. Default Printer





 Make sure your printer is set as the default printer in
 your computer&#039;s settings.










 &amp;nbsp;





 If your issue is still not resolved or you&#039;re unable to follow these
 instructions, contact our troubleshooting experts, who will diagnose the
 specific problem you&#039;re facing. Our certified experts will help you resolve
 the issue over the phone CALL OUR EXPERTS +1-512-885-1530.










 &amp;nbsp;




 &amp;copy; https://printersclan.com



 &amp;nbsp;


--B_ALT_682613f4be32b5.60504265
